# KaminIDE patches — gpui-pre 0.3.8 (zed 279fe070bb389b79652e52065b2f001edcc0b11b)
#
# 1. Expose final Taffy flex line/item geometry, typed fragmentation growth constraints and caller-owned monolithic classification.
# 2. Measured hosts: expose the native containing-block size and resolved edges, preserving CSS percentage padding and content-box sizing in probe and final builds.
# 3. CSS layout: pass measured baselines and intrinsic image sizes into Taffy so flex/grid sizing and alignment use text/image metrics.
# 4. CSS painting: stacking collectors retain DOM order independently of layout; transforms, clipping, gradients and compositing preserve CSS paint contexts.
# 5. Text: retain per-run size, spacing, decorations and vertical layout in shaping/cache keys to prevent reuse across incompatible metrics.
# 6. Tests: retain bundled upstream fonts for SVG regression coverage and import the moved image-fit type explicitly.
# 7. Resolved path scenes: share markup rasterization and exact BGRA conversion with typed tiny-skia geometry, avoiding generated SVG text.
# 8. Host integration: frame capture with an opt-in first-frame latch for WPT convergence diagnostics, animation clock, opt-in prepaint profiling and identity-transformed profiler overlay.
# 9. Window traversal: typed host context scopes replace the need for paint/prepaint TLS and follow canonical paint/deferred snapshots.
# 10. calc-size: carry sizing keyword bases and sizing-box calculations into native intrinsic layout.
# 11. Grid placement: expose completed item row spans from Taffy metadata, preserving implicit lines, source order and dirty-state absence.
#
